// MLOps_Flow — Fragmented Model Flow in the Current Condition (MLOps)
// Manual render: https://app.eraser.io > Diagram-as-code (cloud architecture).
//   Create a NEW canvas named "MLOps_Flow" (canvas name = file
//   name; the cloud architecture syntax has no title line).
// Export the PNG to materials/reports/figures/MLOps_Flow.png
// Icons: every node carries an icon; icon names verified against
//   docs.eraser.io/docs/icons (checked 2026-07-11).
// Reference: Figure III.2 (fig:fragment-mlops), Section III.1.3.
// This diagram depicts the model flow in the condition BEFORE the platform (the
// fragmented status quo): each stage uses a generic ad hoc stack assembled
// manually, so the nodes deliberately do NOT name any platform/components/
// component (the no-tools rule). Domain-agnostic: it names no particular domain.
// Rendering MUST be horizontal (direction right), one chain left to right,
// without deep vertical stacking. Included without \rotatebox in LaTeX.
// Maturity basis (Section II.1.2, subsec:maturity):
// - MLOps level 0 (googlecloud2024mlops): manual script-based process,
//   one-way model handoff, no CI/CD, no active performance monitoring.
// The "Current Maturity Characteristics" group renders that marker on the PNG.
// DELIBERATE SEPARATION: this file shares NOT ONE edge with
// DataOps_Flow.eraser. The disconnect of the model flow from the data flow is
// its main message (the starting point of the domino effect, Section III.1.3). The one-way
// model handoff is marked on the edge Scattered Model Storage > Manual Deployment.

direction right

// Actors
Data Scientist [icon: user, color: gray]
ML Engineer [icon: user, color: gray]

// Fragmented MLOps chain (left to right)
Scattered Feature Engineering [icon: code, color: yellow, label: "Scattered Feature Engineering (notebooks, ad hoc SQL, Python scripts)"]
Isolated Model Development [icon: laptop, color: yellow, label: "Isolated Model Development (local laptop, per-individual Git)"]
Ad Hoc Model Testing [icon: check-circle, color: yellow, label: "Ad Hoc Model Testing (notebooks, spreadsheet calculation)"]
Scattered Model Storage [icon: archive, color: red, label: "Scattered Model Storage (.pkl files, network drive, email)"]
Manual Deployment [icon: upload, color: red, label: "Manual Deployment (code rewrite, SSH)"]
Basic Model Serving [icon: server, color: red, label: "Basic Model Serving (single REST API, cron job)"]
Basic Monitoring [icon: eye, color: red, label: "Basic Monitoring (log files, email alerts)"]

// Maturity marker (MLOps level 0), compact at the right end
Current Maturity Characteristics [icon: eye, color: gray] {
  MLOps Level 0 Marker [icon: alert-triangle, label: "MLOps level 0 (googlecloud2024mlops): manual script-based process, one-way model handoff, no CI/CD, no active performance monitoring"]
}

// Experiment and training flow (managed by the Data Scientist)
Scattered Feature Engineering > Isolated Model Development: ad hoc handoff
Data Scientist > Scattered Feature Engineering: builds features
Data Scientist > Isolated Model Development: develops model
Isolated Model Development > Ad Hoc Model Testing: local validation
Data Scientist > Ad Hoc Model Testing: validates performance
Ad Hoc Model Testing > Scattered Model Storage: stores artifact

// One-way model handoff from experiment to operations (managed by the ML Engineer)
Scattered Model Storage > Manual Deployment: one-way model handoff
ML Engineer > Manual Deployment: handles deployment
Manual Deployment > Basic Model Serving: release to production
ML Engineer > Basic Model Serving: manages serving
Basic Model Serving > Basic Monitoring: tracks performance
ML Engineer > Basic Monitoring: tracks and alerts

// Manual feedback loop
Basic Monitoring > Data Scientist: alerts and retraining
